userid=1372582&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1564695004" alt="Jacob Conwell" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1372582)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacob-conwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1372582); return false;">Jacob Conwell</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/maliceaforethought" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2902864); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2902864&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1564695004" alt="MaliceAforethought" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2902864)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/maliceaforethought" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2902864); return false;">MaliceAforethought</a></span> for reading and giving crit, and thanks to everyone that left feedback in the original discussion thread.</p>
<p>Fun fact that isn't directly stated in the article because I couldn't think of a good place to put it: Those transmissions in the image traveled 28 kilolight-years (28,000 light-years) before reaching Earth and getting detected. This is the earliest transmission from the anomaly that was detected, which means that SCP-3417 has been preaching for at least 28,000 years, and has been alive for longer.</p>
<p><a href="http://kaktuskontainer.wikidot.com/sigma:9volt-scp-3417-original">Original Version of SCP-3417</a></p>
